skill: "redline-diff-analyzer"
sections[3]:
  - "# redline-diff-analyzer\n\nAnalyze a counterparty's redline against the template: classify every change as added, modified or deleted per clause, flag variances against the clause playbook, and propose fallback language from pre-approved ranges. Use every time a draft comes back from a counterparty, before any human reads it.\n\nOwner: role-contract-manager (pod-gna, legal). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[4]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - run_command\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"counterparty redline; controlling template and version; clause playbook clause-playbook.toon (per-clause allowed ranges, fallback language, approval owner); prior correspondence\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/legal/redline-report.toon with changes[] (clause_id, type add|modify|delete, variance severity, fallback), out_of_range[], summary for negotiator\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Identify the controlling template and version for this agreement class; a redline against the wrong template version invalidates the diff and stops the run.\n2. Diff the redline against the template with run_command; segment by clause id from the template's numbering, never by visual paragraph.\n3. Classify each change: added, modified or deleted, with the exact before and after text quoted; a report without quoted text is an opinion, not an analysis.\n4. Compare each changed clause against clause-playbook.toon: inside the allowed range is in-range; outside is out-of-range with severity per playbook class.\n5. Attach the pre-approved fallback language for every out-of-range clause; if the playbook has no fallback, the item goes to out_of_range[] with the approval owner named by the playbook.\n6. Check deletions with extra care: a silently deleted clause (warranty, audit right, limitation) is severity-critical even when the deletion looks tidy.\n7. Produce the negotiator summary: three buckets - acceptable as-is, propose fallback, escalate - with counts and the highest-severity items first.\n8. Write redline-report.toon; emit ask_question to role-general-counsel only for items the playbook itself marks as escalate, and record the negotiation outcome back into the playbook history.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\nescalations to role-general-counsel; outcomes recorded to clause playbook history.\n"
